From d744bb1b1deac913730a69a89a4e05deb305dc17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 22:01:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Split login into admin and lesgever roles

The app had a single shared account with full rights. This adds a second,
restricted role that can view everything and record day-to-day progress,
but cannot manage leerlingen, lesgevers or brevetniveaus.

The real restriction lives in Supabase RLS (the anon key is public in this
static site, so hiding buttons is not security). Roles are stored in
public.app_users and read via the is_admin() / can_record() helpers:

  teachers, pupils, levels, overrides  read: any signed-in user
                                       write: admin only
  achievements, comments               read: any signed-in user
                                       write: admin or teacher

This commit is the UI half. After login the app fetches the role and hides
what the account cannot do: the Lesgevers and Brevetten tabs, the pupil
add/edit form, the per-pupil edit/delete buttons, and lesson drag-and-drop
in the calendar. Ticking off brevetten and writing comments stay available
to both roles. On any failure to read the role, the app falls back to the
restricted role.

Bumps APP_VERSION and the service worker cache to 5.1.0 so existing PWA
installs pick up the new shell.

