Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Show every name in the calendar and ask before moving a
 student
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two problems, both surfaced by the jump from 16 to 78 leerlingen.

The week grid rendered only the first five names per day and appended
"+N meer". Wednesday now holds 37 students, so picking a lesgever changed
five alphabetically-similar names and looked like the filter did nothing.
It was filtering correctly the whole time — you just couldn't see it.

Day columns now list everyone, scrolling within the column, and carry a
tally that states what the filter did: "37 leerlingen" unfiltered,
"22 van 37" when a lesgever is selected. The filter itself is labelled,
highlighted while active, has a clear-button, and is remembered between
visits. Selecting a lesgever who has nobody that day says so rather than
showing a bare dash. The day-detail modal gained the same tally.

Dragging a student to another day always created a one-off move. That is
still often right ("ziek deze week"), but the common case is a permanent
switch, and the app was guessing. On drop it now asks: "Alleen deze week"
keeps the old override behaviour, "Vanaf nu altijd" writes the new day to
pupils.weekday and clears an override that has become redundant.

Dragging stays admin-only, matching the RLS rules — pupils.weekday and
overrides are both admin-write.

Bumps APP_VERSION and the service worker cache to 5.2.0.

